Illmari is a late-60s half-elf male, with black, slicked back hair and scars on his face. He has a raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]].

Illmari is the current proprietor of the [[Sin and Tonic]] and the founder of the mercenary group [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. He was one of the first to capitalize on hearing the [[Voidsong]], collecting like-minded people to investigate its source and meaning.

The founder of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]], [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Illmari Vaino|Illmari]] is better known around [[Sin and Tonic]] as a cook — a tension between those two identities that those who know him tend not to press on.

He was born in [[Geography/Velthara/index|Velthara]], and his family moved to [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]] at some point after. He ran an adventuring company that, as adventuring was swallowed up by the orgs, tried to turn mercenary. Most of his party died in an accident around the time the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] appeared. Only Illmari and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Elias Ramsey|Elias]] came out of it, and they came out with treasure enough for Illmari to buy the [[Sin and Tonic]]. He then called publicly for anyone willing to look into the song, and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Flynn|Flynn]] and one other joined him near the start, followed by [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Dura Oil-Drinker|Dura]] and others. He was never an outgoing man, and little of his private life is on record.

Illmari is missing. He left the bar the night of the party at Teller's Run and has not come back. He usually says where he is going, and none of Ginny, Anouk, Anaïs, Dura or Elias knows where he went.

The [[Org/The Harlequins/People/The Master of Ceremonies|Master of Ceremonies]] of the [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]] says Illmari is still alive, and that what has become of him is not his to tell.
